 "purpose": "The sentence machine: a sentence structure times words from the word list gives a fully analysed Dutch sentence.",
 "details": "As with word problems, the structure (a code from the leerlijn, such as o_pv_lv or bwb_pv_o_mv_lv) says which parts exist and in which order; the word list (inhoud/taal/woorden.json) supplies the words, so the machine knows both the sentence parts and the word classes. The finite verb agrees with the subject (singular/plural) and the tense; the object fits the verb (read a book, eat an apple). Eleven simple structures (including inversion, a question, a perfect tense with an auxiliary, a predicate with a linking verb, and 'aan/voor' indirect objects) and five compound ones with two pv's (en, shared subject, dat, terwijl, and terwijl fronted). A Bouwer builds the sentence piece by piece; choices that do not fit raise Opnieuw and are retried (up to 200 or 400 times) until the sentence is valid and fits the screen width.",
 "module_docstring": "De zinnenmachine: een zinsbouw × woorden uit de woordenlijst (inhoud/taal/woorden.json) = een volledig ontlede zin.",
